rogram\nCongress\nHemaSphere\nAbout EHA\nSearch\nJoin EHA\nLogin\nHemaSphere\nHome\nResearch & Innovation\nHemaSphere\nLeft Sidebar\n3 min read · April 30, 2025\nApril 30, 2025\nShare\nResearch & Innovation\nHemaSphere\nSpecialized Working Groups\nGrants\nTopics-in-Focus program\nStay at the forefront of cutting-edge research with EHA’s open access, peer-reviewed journal.\nWith a preliminary 2025 Impact Factor of 11.3, placing it #8 in indexed hematology journals worldwide, HemaSphere is an invaluable resource for hematologists at every career stage.\nOur continuous online publications support the global hematology community by sharing:\nResults of high-impact basic, translational, and clinical hematology research\nInsightful review articles\nClinical practice guidelines\nReports of new therapies\nRecommendations for future research and clinical applications\nDiscussions on European policy\nAnd more\nWe also provide the hematology community with a friction-free route to publishing and publication access through our:\nFast and constructive review process\n100% open access content\nLow publication fees\nLatest issue\nExplore this month’s HemaSphere issue, featuring a broad range of hematology papers and insightful discussions on trending topics.\nHemaSphere podcast\nListen to the latest HemaSphere podcast and enjoy lighthearted conversations about the research stories behind the publications.\nThis audio companion to our official journal is available on a range of podcast platforms, and we launch new episodes regularly.\nCall for novel findings\nHemaSphere is interested in high-impact studies that share novel findings.\nIf your study fits this description, please feel free to submit it online for our consideration. HemaSphere does not charge any submission fees.\nDiscounted publishing fees for EHA members\nActive EHA members can benefit from discounted publishing fees in HemaSphere. Interested in publishing at this discounted rate? Learn more about joining EHA.\nSubmit your paper\nWe welcome your submission. On average, it takes us just 10 days to make a first decision. If you have a manuscript that you think would be a good fit for our journal, please submit your paper. HemaSphere receives all manuscript submissions online.\nRemember, active EHA members benefit from discounted publishing fees.\nHemaSphere Editorial Board\nHemaSphere’s Editorial Board is responsible for:\nReviewing and selecting manuscripts for publication\nGuiding our journal’s quality, strategy, and growth\nYou can find out more about the remit and composition of this body on the HemaSphere Editorial Board page.\nJournal metrics\nAs a premier hematology information resource, HemaSphere has:\nA preliminary 2025 Journal Impact Factor (JIF) of 11.3 (source: Journal Citation Reports, Clarivate)\nA Scopus 2025 CiteScore of 6.9\nIt is also:\nFully indexed in PubMed Central (PMC)\nIndexed in Science Citation Expanded Index (SCIE)—Hematology and Clinical Medicine (Clarivate Analytics)\nListed in the Directory of Open Access Journals (DOAJ)\nOur publishing partner\nHemaSphere is published by the global research and education specialist, Wiley. Their range of digital and physical platforms enables us to bring HemaSphere to the widest possible audience.\nShare\nResearch & Innovation\nHemaSphere\nSpecialized Working Groups\nGrants\nTopics-in-Focus program\nJoin EHA\nFull membership\nJunior membership\n60-day trial\nGet involved\nCareer development\nScientific meetings\nAbout us\nMission and vision\nJobs\nSponsor EHA\nContact us\nFollow us\nPrivacy statement\nTerms and conditions\nSubscribe\nCopyright © 2026\nBecome an EHA Mentor\nEHA Mentorship Program\nDiscover the rewards of mentoring\nApply by October 29\nApply today",
